      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "{\u0022paragraphs\u0022:[[{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022The first risk is that supply constraints limit how quickly demand converts into revenue, since management called supply chain the governor of near-term revenue for the next several quarters.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:3},{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022That risk would be confirmed by fourth-quarter revenue landing below the $1.93 billion low end of the guidance range, or non-GAAP earnings per share below the $3.34 low end of guidance, in a quarter where management guided to growth of about 37% at the midpoint.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:1}],[{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022The second risk is that profitability was lifted by onetime tariff effects this year that management said will not repeat.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:3},{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022That risk would be confirmed by gross margin falling below the 65.87% of the latest quarter while revenue still arrives inside the $1.93 billion to $1.95 billion guidance range.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:1}],[{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022The third risk is that growth leans on AI infrastructure spending, with wireline revenue passing wireless revenue for the first time.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:2},{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022The Communications Solutions Group supplied $1,345 million of the $1.85 billion of quarterly revenue.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:1},{\u0022sentence\u0022:\u0022That risk would be confirmed by Communications Solutions Group revenue in the next quarter falling below the $1,345 million it posted in the latest quarter, reversing a trend of 43% growth on a year earlier.\u0022,\u0022document\u0022:1}]]}"
